{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## 5. Baseline maintenance: the decision, its history, and the bug it exposed\n\nThe two ratchets keep committed lists: .github/complexity-baseline.json (per-function McCabe ceilings, shrink-only) and .github/mechanism-baseline.json (censused mechanisms by kind and name). Removing something leaves a stale row. For the complexity list, stale rows are tolerated by make lint and CI since bug dystopian-bardlike-basil (d319-a094-4ee7-4549) fixed the contradiction in August. For the mechanism list they are not: tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree asserts set(baseline) | admitted == live, so a change that deletes a censused mechanism must also drop its row, and the only tool that drops rows is --update-stale (precedent: commit 81da792, which retired the HLC switch). AGENTS.md calls that flag maintenance-only.\n\nHistory of why hand edits are prohibited: task 47e9 (janitor 2026-08-06) locked the complexity baseline with a CI step (--lock) that diffs the change against main's merge base and rejects any added key, administrator force-submit being the designed override; a path re-spell is a remove plus an add and cannot be told from a smuggled ceiling. The mechanism baseline has no CI lock; the prohibition is the operator's 2026-09-06 ruling on celadon-computable-smelts (a1f1-a30d-2d50-4f5a): mechanisms must not require exception routes, agents abuse exception paths, the baseline must not become contributor-editable; the sanctioned paths are \"land it, change nothing\" for reductions and the mechanism-ok marker for additions. Change 2658's agent hand-added two rows to get past the tests and that was recorded as a guidance violation.\n\nDefect found: _run_update_stale (scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:177-195) refuses on compare()'s marker-blind has_regression (scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:45-57), while the gate's evaluate() and the unit tests honour markers. Consequence, proven live on origin/main 4c77d6f3e96f in a scratch worktree: seven marker-admitted mechanisms already exist without baseline rows (autouse_fixture::tests/conftest.py::_one_engine_root and six ci_gate entries), so --update-stale refuses on an unmodified checkout, which blocks every one of the ten breaking-pass stories that delete a mechanism. The one-function fix (replace the compare/has_regression refusal with evaluate(current, baseline, markers_for(repo_root)) and refuse on a nonzero code) was applied in the scratch worktree: --check and --update-stale exit 0 with the baseline byte-identical, and a scratch regression test failed on the unfixed script at assert rc == 0 and passed with the fix (35 passed with the existing 33). Filed as bug amoeboid-amateur-guillemot (1768-5b6f-958a-43e9, priority 1, discovered_from a1f1) with the diff and evidence in its first comment; the overlap, editor, reconciler, LLM-leftovers, HMAC, MCP and config epics depend on it.\n\nOperator decisions (approved 2026-09-07): (1) the same-change drain stays the rule for removals; AGENTS.md and docs/architecture.md are reworded and --update-stale made marker-aware by the bug fix; (2) the reconciler package-move story keeps its six-key complexity-baseline re-spell and the operator force-submits that one change once the lock step is its only red CI item, the implementing agent handing off and never overriding; (3) the 29-key mechanism-baseline re-spell in the test-package rename is a sanctioned one-time maintenance edit named in the commit message, with a reviewer check posted on the story (strip the moved prefix, sort name and value, diff main against the change, expect no difference). Additional finding from the experiments: the complexity map must be re-sorted, not just substituted, because reconciler/ sorts after the underscore-prefixed keys and an unsorted file fails --check."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788839679715236001,"uuid":"560844d0-a037-4788-9dc7-829381f407bd"}